within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.P_AntiparasiticProductsInsecticidesAndRepellents.P01C_AgentsAgainstLeishmaniasisAndTrypanosomiasis.P01CX04_Miltefosine;
model Miltefosine "Miltefosine — default model: Miltefosine_Pali2020_reference"
  extends Miltefosine_Pali2020_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of miltefosine: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.P_AntiparasiticProductsInsecticidesAndRepellents.P01C_AgentsAgainstLeishmaniasisAndTrypanosomiasis.P01CX04_Miltefosine.Miltefosine_Pali2020_reference\">Miltefosine_Pali2020_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of miltefosine in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Miltefosine_Pali2020_reference</code></li><li><code>Miltefosine_Madu2023_PD_pbmc_concentration</code></li><li><code>Miltefosine_Verrest2024_PD_parasite_load</code></li></ul><h4>About miltefosine</h4><p>Miltefosine is a phospholipid drug used as an antiprotozoal agent against leishmaniasis and trypanosomiasis, and it also has antifungal, antibacterial and anticancer activity. It is an approved medicine, included on the WHO essential medicines list, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q411787\">Wikidata Q411787</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Miltefosine\">Miltefosine</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 3024000, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Miltefosine;
